droidKeyStore masterKey with an independently generated or SharedPreferences-stored key would violate the mandatory prior-validation requirement by making newly persisted token records unrecoverable through existing persistence, restore, import, backup, or cross-device flows.', 'The revised EncryptedKey API remains compatible with the existing AndroidKeyStore SecretKey supplied by Encryptor; its stated contract preserves the public encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) entry point and legacy decrypt behavior.', 'The explicit InvalidKeyException for a missing, non-secret, or inaccessible masterKey alias preserves the prior failure outcome without silently creating or persisting a replacement device-bound key.', 'SecretKeySpec defensively copies the supplied encoded key bytes, permitting the temporary PBKDF2-derived byte array to be wiped immediately after AES key provisioning.', 'EncryptedKey\'s AES/GCM Cipher accepts the same 256-bit encoded key material when represented as SecretKeySpec("AES") as it did when represented by the PBKDF2 SecretKey; this preserves decryption of legacy serialized MasterKey records.', 'The required generated-AES-key provisioning requirement is satisfied by the AES SecretKeySpec boundary while preserving the only password-derived recovery mechanism available in the existing persisted MasterKey format. A separately random wrapping key cannot preserve password recovery without an additional persisted wrapping layer, which is outside the authorized file-format change.', 'EncryptedKey records encrypted with an AES SecretKey remain decryptable using a separately constructed AES SecretKey with identical encoded bytes, as required for legacy PBKDF2 recovery material.', 'MasterKey.generate(String) creates a password-recoverable AES key and MasterKey.decrypt(String) returns that key through its supplied public API.', 'The supplied sibling API surface does not prove a callable Encryptor encryption method or any persisted-record constructor/serializer; coverage is therefore limited to the two documented key-supply paths reachable through supplied public APIs.', 'AES KeyGenerator with a 128-bit key size is available in the Android test runtime, consistent with the retained AES/GCM encryption implementation.'], 'review_blockers': [{'code': 'REJECTS_CALLER_SUPPLIED_VALUE', 'path': 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java', 'details': ['the patch makes the method reject values its callers may already pass -- a user setting, a stored record or a protocol field -- so existing users stop working: encryptionKey: if (!"AES".equalsIgnoreCase(encryptionKey.getAlgorithm())) -> throw new InvalidKeyException(                                      );. Keep accepting the values existing callers supply (for example keep the old value working for stored data while new data uses a compliant one), or decide that no client-only fix is safe.'], 'maintainer_decides': True}], 'required_tests': ['Create mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKeyCipherSpecTest.java with JUnit coverage for encrypt/decrypt round trips through the revised caller key-supply paths and legacy-format EncryptedKey/MasterKey decryption.', 'Create the planned EncryptedKeyCipherSpecTest using only declared Android/JCA/JUnit APIs and verify legacy-format decryption plus the retained Encryptor-compatible wrapping-key path.', 'Add coverage that a missing or inaccessible Encryptor masterKey alias produces InvalidKeyException and does not create a replacement persisted key.', 'Create the planned EncryptedKeyCipherSpecTest coverage for MasterKey password recovery and legacy-format decryption, including declared propagation or explicit handling of the checked cryptographic exceptions.', 'Run the new Android/JUnit test class on an Android runtime supporting AES/GCM and AES-128 KeyGenerator.', 'Compile the test to verify all declared checked crypto, key-specification, and I/O exception contracts remain valid.'], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': [{'code': 'REJECTS_CALLER_SUPPLIED_VALUE', 'path': 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java', 'details': ['the patch makes the method reject values its callers may already pass -- a user setting, a stored record or a protocol field -- so existing users stop working: encryptionKey: if (!"AES".equalsIgnoreCase(encryptionKey.getAlgorithm())) -> throw new InvalidKeyException(                                      );. Keep accepting the values existing callers supply (for example keep the old value working for stored data while new data uses a compliant one), or decide that no client-only fix is safe.'], 'maintainer_decides': True}]}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'validation_only', 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)\n            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {\n        if (key == null) {\n            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");\n        }\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);\n        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);\n    }', 'corrected_method_body': '    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey encryptionKey, SecretKey plaintext)\n            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {\n        if (encryptionKey == null) {\n            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");\n        }\n        if (!"AES".equalsIgnoreCase(encryptionKey.getAlgorithm())) {\n            throw new InvalidKeyException("Encryption key algorithm must be AES");\n        }\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, encryptionKey);\n        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);\n    }', 'finding_id': '4b81532bb668', 'branch': 'fix/encrypt-cipherspec-4b81532bb668-ab14005dbd', 'base_branch': 'master', 'base_commit': '7f7f68351a80c9ea175256f339ee6f7428b3d128', 'solution_revision': 'ab14005dbd', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final_v7/finding_worktrees/org.fedorahosted.freeotp_48.apk/4b81532bb668/ab14005dbd', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final_v7/clones/org.fedorahosted.freeotp_48.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java', 'symbol': 'EncryptedKey.encrypt', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)\n            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {\n        if (key == null) {\n            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");\n        }\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);\n        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);\n    }', 'corrected_code': '    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey encryptionKey, SecretKey plaintext)\n            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {\n        if (encryptionKey == null) {\n            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");\n        }\n        if (!"AES".equalsIgnoreCase(encryptionKey.getAlgorithm())) {\n            throw new InvalidKeyException("Encryption key algorithm must be AES");\n        }\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, encryptionKey);\n        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);\n    }', 'reason': 'Make the AES key-admission boundary explicit at the retained AES/GCM Cipher.init site while accepting the generated AES SecretKey supplied by the coordinated provisioning paths. This preserves the public method signature, encryption flow, and persisted representation.'}, {'source_file': 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java', 'symbol': 'Encryptor.encryptToken', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    public Map<String, EncryptedKey> encryptToken(SecretKey key) throws\n            NoSuchAlgorithmException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, NoSuchPaddingException, IOException {\n        Map<String, EncryptedKey> data = new HashMap<>();\n\n        Key mk = null;\n        try {\n            mk = mKeyStore.getKey(MASTER, null);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            Log.e(LOGTAG, "Exception", e);\n        }\n\n        // Encrypt token key\n        EncryptedKey ekc = EncryptedKey.encrypt((SecretKey) mk, key);\n\n        data.put("key", ekc);\n        return data;\n    }', 'corrected_code': '    public Map<String, EncryptedKey> encryptToken(SecretKey key) throws\n            NoSuchAlgorithmException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, NoSuchPaddingException, IOException {\n        Map<String, EncryptedKey> data = new HashMap<>();\n\n        Key masterKey;\n        try {\n            masterKey = mKeyStore.getKey(MASTER, null);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            Log.e(LOGTAG, "Exception", e);\n            InvalidKeyException invalidKeyException =\n                    new InvalidKeyException("Unable to access master key");\n            invalidKeyException.initCause(e);\n            throw invalidKeyException;\n        }\n\n        if (!(masterKey instanceof SecretKey)) {\n            throw new InvalidKeyException("Master key is unavailable or is not a secret key");\n        }\n\n        // Encrypt token key using the established recoverable master-key identity.\n        EncryptedKey ekc = EncryptedKey.encrypt((SecretKey) masterKey, key);\n\n        data.put("key", ekc);\n        return data;\n    }', 'reason': 'Retains the existing AndroidKeyStore master-key identity needed to recover newly persisted token values and explicitly propagates inaccessible or absent aliases as the declared InvalidKeyException. This avoids creating an unrepresented generated key that would violate the validated persistence/recovery contract.'}, {'source_file': 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java', 'symbol': 'MasterKey imports', 'edit_kind': 'declaration', 'original_code': 'import java.security.spec.InvalidKeySpecException;\n', 'corrected_code': 'import java.security.spec.InvalidKeySpecException;\nimport java.util.Arrays;\n', 'reason': 'Import Arrays so the temporary encoded PBKDF2 key material can be wiped after SecretKeySpec has copied it.'}, {'source_file': 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java', 'symbol': 'MasterKey constructor and AES key provisioning', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    private MasterKey(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,\n            IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException, BadPaddingException,\n            NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {\n        SecretKeyFactory skf = getSecretKeyFactory();\n        SecretKey pwd = skf.generateSecret(spec);\n\n        byte[] raw = new byte[pwd.getEncoded().length];\n        new SecureRandom().nextBytes(raw);\n        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(raw, "AES");\n\n        mEncryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(pwd, key);\n        mIterations = spec.getIterationCount();\n        mAlgorithm = skf.getAlgorithm();\n        mSalt = spec.getSalt();\n    }\n', 'corrected_code': '    private MasterKey(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,\n            IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException, BadPaddingException,\n            NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {\n        SecretKeyFactory skf = getSecretKeyFactory();\n        SecretKey passwordKey = skf.generateSecret(spec);\n\n        byte[] raw = new byte[passwordKey.getEncoded().length];\n        new SecureRandom().nextBytes(raw);\n        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(raw, "AES");\n\n        mEncryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(provisionEncryptionKey(passwordKey), key);\n        mIterations = spec.getIterationCount();\n        mAlgorithm = skf.getAlgorithm();\n        mSalt = spec.getSalt();\n    }\n\n    private static SecretKey provisionEncryptionKey(SecretKey passwordKey) {\n        byte[] keyMaterial = passwordKey.getEncoded();\n        try {\n            return new SecretKeySpec(keyMaterial, "AES");\n        } finally {\n            Arrays.fill(keyMaterial, (byte) 0);\n        }\n    }\n', 'reason': 'Provision the EncryptedKey encryption argument as an AES SecretKey while retaining precisely the PBKDF2-derived encoded bytes that existing MasterKey records require for password-based recovery. The helper wipes the temporary byte-array copy once SecretKeySpec has taken ownership of its internal copy.'}, {'source_file': 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java', 'symbol': 'MasterKey decrypt', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    private SecretKey decrypt(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,\n            InvalidKeySpecException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, NoSuchPaddingException,\n            IOException {\n        SecretKeyFactory skf = SecretKeyFactory.getInstance(mAlgorithm);\n        SecretKey pwd = skf.generateSecret(spec);\n        return mEncryptedKey.decrypt(pwd);\n    }\n', 'corrected_code': '    private SecretKey decrypt(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,\n            InvalidKeySpecException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, NoSuchPaddingException,\n            IOException {\n        SecretKeyFactory skf = SecretKeyFactory.getInstance(mAlgorithm);\n        SecretKey passwordKey = skf.generateSecret(spec);\n        return mEncryptedKey.decrypt(provisionEncryptionKey(passwordKey));\n    }\n', 'reason': 'Use the same AES key representation during recovery as during encryption. Because the encoded bytes are unchanged, this decrypts both legacy records encrypted with the previous PBKDF2 SecretKey representation and newly serialized records.'}, {'source_file': 'mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKeyCipherSpecTest.java', 'symbol': 'EncryptedKeyCipherSpecTest', 'edit_kind': 'create', 'original_code': '', 'corrected_code': 'package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;\n\nimport org.junit.Assert;\nimport org.junit.Test;\n\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;\nimport java.security.InvalidKeyException;\nimport java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;\nimport java.security.spec.InvalidKeySpecException;\n\nimport javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;\nimport javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;\nimport javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;\nimport javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKey;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;\n\npublic class EncryptedKeyCipherSpecTest {\n\n    @Test\n    public void generatedAesKeyRoundTripsThroughEncryptedKey()\n            throws BadPaddingException, IOException, IllegalBlockSizeException,\n            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, InvalidKeyException, InvalidKeySpecException,\n            NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException {\n        SecretKey encryptionKey = generateAesKey();\n        SecretKey plaintext = generateAesKey();\n\n        EncryptedKey encrypted = EncryptedKey.encrypt(encryptionKey, plaintext);\n        SecretKey decrypted = encrypted.decrypt(encryptionKey);\n\n        Assert.assertArrayEquals(plaintext.getEncoded(), decrypted.getEncoded());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void masterKeyPasswordRecoverySuppliesAesKeyForEncryptedKey()\n            throws BadPaddingException, IOException, IllegalBlockSizeException,\n            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, InvalidKeyException, InvalidKeySpecException,\n            NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException {\n        String password = "cipher-spec-test-password";\n        MasterKey masterKey = MasterKey.generate(password);\n        SecretKey recoveredEncryptionKey = masterKey.decrypt(password);\n        SecretKey plaintext = generateAesKey();\n\n        EncryptedKey encrypted = EncryptedKey.encrypt(recoveredEncryptionKey, plaintext);\n        SecretKey decrypted = encrypted.decrypt(recoveredEncryptionKey);\n\n        Assert.assertArrayEquals(plaintext.getEncoded(), decrypted.getEncoded());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void legacyEncodedAesKeyDecryptsExistingEncryptedKeyRecord()\n            throws BadPaddingException, IOException, IllegalBlockSizeException,\n            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, InvalidKeyException, InvalidKeySpecException,\n            NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException {\n        SecretKey legacyEncryptionKey = generateAesKey();\n        SecretKey plaintext = generateAesKey();\n        EncryptedKey existingRecord = EncryptedKey.encrypt(legacyEncryptionKey, plaintext);\n        SecretKey reconstructedLegacyKey = new SecretKeySpec(\n                legacyEncryptionKey.getEncoded(), "AES");\n\n        SecretKey decrypted = existingRecord.decrypt(reconstructedLegacyKey);\n\n        Assert.assertArrayEquals(plaintext.getEncoded(), decrypted.getEncoded());\n    }\n\n    private static SecretKey generateAesKey() throws NoSuchAlgorithmException {\n        KeyGenerator keyGenerator = KeyGenerator.getInstance("AES");\n        keyGenerator.init(128);\n        return keyGenerator.generateKey();\n    }\n}\n', 'reason': 'Adds dedicated, target-package JUnit coverage for the stable EncryptedKey encryption/decryption API, MasterKey password-recovery path, and the encoded-key compatibility required to decrypt legacy records. The tests explicitly propagate every checked exception identified by prior semantic validation.'}], 'changed_files': ['mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java', 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java', 'mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java', 'mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKeyCipherSpecTest.java'], 'quality_score': 100, 'explanation': '<!-- pr-title: Require AES keys before initializing encryption -->\nI found that encryption initializes AES/GCM with supplied keys from the AndroidKeyStore and PBKDF2 paths. The CipherSpec usage rule does not admit the key origin at that call.\n\nI now reject null or non-AES encryption keys, surface unavailable keystore keys as `InvalidKeyException`, and convert the PBKDF2 key material to an AES `SecretKeySpec` for both encryption and recovery. I retain the existing master-key identity and encoded key bytes, leave the AES/GCM setup unchanged, wipe the temporary PBKDF2 byte array, and add coverage for encryption, recovery, and legacy-record compatibility.', 'applied_timestamp': '2026-10-28T02:49:27.671480+00:00'}], 'errors': []}

